/-- Source atomicity alone does not make the sign-oriented endpoint target
survive the finite no-prime/atomic filter.

This is the guardrail for the next producer step: the raw `E-1` endpoint move
is not itself the filtered connectedness theorem.  The SU(7) grammar still has
to generate completion/repair room rather than merely applying this fixed
endpoint-code shift. -/
theorem su7A6_sourceOrientedEndpointTarget_filter_not_forced_by_source_atomicity :
    let source :=
      su7A6EndpointSourceLabel 5 7 (rawCodePairResidualEnergy 10 5 7)
    natMultiplicativelyAtomicCheck
        (su7A6ConcreteEndpointSourceGrammar.leftCodeOf source) = true ∧
      natMultiplicativelyAtomicCheck
        (su7A6ConcreteEndpointSourceGrammar.rightCodeOf source) = true ∧
